{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MsMEeyWrAhY8guCSyPMtPa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n2\t\n3\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n4\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n5\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n6\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n7\t\n8\t    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n9\t    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n10\t    Request Method:  GET\n11\t    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n12\t    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n13\t    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n14\t\n15\t### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n16\t\n17\t$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n18\t    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n19\thttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n20\t\n21\t$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\n22\tHTTP/2 400\n23\tcontent-type: application/json\n24\tcache-control: no-store\n25\t\n26\t{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n27\t\n28\t    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n29\t    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n30\t    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n31\t\n32\t### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n33\t\n34\t2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n35\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n36\t{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n37\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n38\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n39\t2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n40\t2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n41\t2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a7877f0-14a6-428e-9156-c370b39b9792","uuid":"baec5f8c-3b06-4ced-896f-ba2c458971d7","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:23:18.967Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-j23kGR/logs/connect-attempt.log","content":"### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MsMEeyWrAhY8guCSyPMtPa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBZoRVzbcYs4Vcp2DUJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nxhy58mg5JgE43iweASD6G","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-j23kGR/logs/support-tickets.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":23296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a7877f0-14a6-428e-9156-c370b39b9792","uuid":"1785fd63-e396-4f3a-9570-8bf4b4d8eff2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:23:19.146Z","request_id":"req_011CgSBZo9tAV9Hnwp427uZ7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Nxhy58mg5JgE43iweASD6G":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-j23kGR/logs/support-tickets.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nxhy58mg5JgE43iweASD6G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n2\t\n3\t## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n4\t\n5\t> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n6\t> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n7\t> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n8\t> Safari and Chrome.\n9\t\n10\tReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\n11\tweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\n12\tgotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n13\t\n14\t## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n15\t\n16\t> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n17\t> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n18\t> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n19\t> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n20\t> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n21\t\n22\tChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n23\t\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n24\t`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\n25\tlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\n26\tbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\n27\tsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\n28\tIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\n29\tathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n30\t`connect-attempt.log`).\n31\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a7877f0-14a6-428e-9156-c370b39b9792","uuid":"794e2b22-e28d-4878-b8f5-a05518c61279","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:23:19.153Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-j23kGR/logs/support-tickets.md","content":"# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Nxhy58mg5JgE43iweASD6G","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
